.TH FGREP 1 "May 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fgrep \- print lines matching a fixed string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fgrep
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.I PATTERN
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fgrep
is equivalent to
.BR "grep \-F" .
It interprets each
.I PATTERN
as a fixed string to be matched literally, with no regular-expression
metacharacters.  It is provided as a symbolic link to
.BR grep (1)
and accepts all of the same options.
.PP
.B fgrep
is deprecated by POSIX; new scripts should use
.B grep \-F
instead.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
See
.BR grep (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grep (1),
.BR egrep (1)
